/-!
# Liftings of the quotient graph of a group acting on a tree

Let a group `G` act on a tree `T` without inversions, with quotient graph `B = T / G`
(`GTree.quotient`) and projection `q : T → B` (`GTree.quotientMap`). The fibres of `q` are the
`G`-orbits, and `B` is connected.

A lifting (`GTree.Lifting`) consists of a spanning tree of `B`, a lift of every vertex of `B` to
`T`, a lift of every dart of `B` issuing from the lift of its source, and for every dart `y` an
element `twist y` of `G` carrying the lift of the reverse of `y` to the reverse of the lift of
`y`. The elements `twist y` are trivial on the darts of the spanning tree and satisfy
`twist (rev y) = (twist y)⁻¹`. The lift of a dart `y` ends at the translate by `twist y` of the
lift of the target of `y` (`GTree.Lifting.tgt_dart`), and the lift of the reverse of `y` is the
translate by `(twist y)⁻¹` of the reverse of the lift of `y` (`GTree.Lifting.dart_rev`); in
particular the lifts of the darts of the spanning tree join lifted vertices
(`GTree.Lifting.tgt_dart_of_mem`) and are closed under reversal
(`GTree.Lifting.dart_rev_of_mem`), so that they lift the spanning tree. Distinct vertices and
distinct darts of `B` have distinct lifts, and every dart of `T` issuing from a lifted vertex is a
translate of a lifted dart by an element of the stabilizer of that vertex
(`GTree.Lifting.exists_smul_dart_eq`). The stabilizer of a lifted dart lies in that of the lift of
its source, conjugation by `twist y` relates the stabilizers of `dart (rev y)` and `dart y`, and
`G` is generated by the stabilizers of the lifted vertices together with the elements `twist y`
(`GTree.Lifting.iSup_stabilizer_sup_closure_range_twist`).

This is the data of the explicit construction of the quotient graph of groups in
Kapovich–Weidmann–Myasnikov, Remark 2.7: the lifted vertices and tree darts form their lift `T₁`
of a maximal subtree, and the elements `(twist y)⁻¹` are their elements `t_v`. There one dart of
each geometric edge outside the tree is lifted; here both orientations are lifted, the lift of
the second one being the translate by `(twist y)⁻¹` of the reverse of the lift of the first.
Liftings exist for every spanning tree of `B` and every choice of the lift of one vertex
(`GTree.exists_lifting`): the spanning tree is lifted along its tree paths from the prescribed
vertex, and the other darts are lifted with their sources at lifted vertices.

The group is generated by the stabilizers of the lifted vertices together with the elements
`twist y` (`GTree.Lifting.iSup_stabilizer_sup_closure_range_twist`; for the fundamental group of
a graph of groups this is Kapovich–Weidmann–Myasnikov, Proposition 2.4 (3)). Conversely, let
`R` be a set of vertices of `B` and `Y` a set of darts between them, closed under reversal, and
let `K b`, for `b` in `R`, be subgroups of the stabilizers of the lifted vertices containing the
stabilizers of the lifted darts of `Y` issuing from them. The pairs of a vertex `b` of `B` and a
left coset of `K b ⊓ G_{vertex b}` are the vertices of a graph with the darts of `T`, the
translate `g • dart y` of a lifted dart of `Y` issuing from the coset of `g` at the source of `y`.
Sending the coset of `g` at `b` to `g • vertex b` is a morphism to `T` which is the identity on
darts; as `T` is a tree, it is injective on the vertices of each connected component. If the
vertices of `R` are joined inside the spanning tree and `Y`, and the subgroups `K b` and the
elements `twist y` for `y` in `Y` generate `G`, then all the cosets at a vertex of `R` lie in one
component, so each `K b` is the whole stabilizer
(`GTree.Lifting.eq_stabilizer_vertex_of_closure_eq_top`).

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting`: a lifting of the quotient graph to the tree.
* `TauCeti.GTree.exists_lifting`: liftings exist, with any spanning tree and any base lift.
* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.tgt_dart`: the lift of a dart ends at a translate of a lifted vertex.
* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.exists_smul_dart_eq`: every dart issuing from a lifted vertex is a
  translate of a lifted dart by an element of the stabilizer of that vertex.
* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.stabilizer_dart_rev`, `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.stabilizer_dart`:
  conjugation by `twist` relates the stabilizers of the lifts of mutually reverse darts.
* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.iSup_stabilizer_sup_closure_range_twist`: `G` is generated by the lifted
  vertex stabilizers and the elements `twist y`.
* `TauCeti.GTree.Lifting.eq_stabilizer_vertex_of_closure_eq_top`: subgroups of the stabilizers
  of the lifted vertices containing the stabilizers of the lifted darts and generating `G`
  together with the elements of the lifting are the whole stabilizers.

## References

* I. Kapovich, R. Weidmann and A. Myasnikov, *Foldings, graphs of groups and the membership
  problem*, Internat. J. Algebra Comput. 15 (2005), §2, Propositions 2.4 (3) and 2.6 and
  Remark 2.7.
* J.-P. Serre, *Trees*, Chapter I, §3.1 and §5.4.
-/

public section

universe u v w

namespace TauCeti

open SerreGraph _root_.MulAction

namespace GTree

variable {G : Type w} [Group G] (T : GTree.{u, v} G)

/-- A lifting of the quotient graph `T / G` of a `G`-tree to the tree: a spanning tree of the
quotient, a lift of every vertex, a lift of every dart issuing from the lift of its source, and
for every dart `y` an element `twist y` of `G` mapping the lift of the reverse of `y` to the
reverse of the lift of `y`. The elements `twist y` are trivial on the spanning tree, so that the
lifts of its darts are closed under reversal and join lifted vertices. -/
@[ext] structure Lifting where
  /-- The spanning tree of the quotient graph. -/
  tree : T.quotient.SpanningTree
  /-- The lift of a vertex of the quotient graph. -/
  vertex : T.quotient.V → T.V
  /-- The lift of a dart of the quotient graph. -/
  dart : T.quotient.E → T.E
  /-- The element of the group attached to a dart of the quotient graph. -/
  twist : T.quotient.E → G
  /-- The lift of a vertex lies over it. -/
  quotientMap_vertex : ∀ b, T.quotientMap.mapV (vertex b) = b
  /-- The lift of a dart lies over it. -/
  quotientMap_dart : ∀ y, T.quotientMap.mapE (dart y) = y
  /-- The lift of a dart issues from the lift of its source. -/
  src_dart : ∀ y, T.src (dart y) = vertex (T.quotient.src y)
  /-- The element of a dart maps the lift of its reverse to the reverse of its lift. -/
  twist_smul_dart_rev : ∀ y, twist y • dart (T.quotient.rev y) = T.rev (dart y)
  /-- The element of the reverse dart is the inverse. -/
  twist_rev : ∀ y, twist (T.quotient.rev y) = (twist y)⁻¹
  /-- The elements of the darts of the spanning tree are trivial. -/
  twist_eq_one : ∀ y ∈ tree.darts, twist y = 1

attribute [simp] Lifting.quotientMap_vertex Lifting.quotientMap_dart Lifting.src_dart
  Lifting.twist_rev Lifting.twist_eq_one

/-! ### Existence of liftings -/

variable {T}

/-- A lift of a dart of the quotient graph with a prescribed source in the orbit of its source. -/
private noncomputable def liftDart {a : T.V} {y : T.quotient.E}
    (h : T.quotient.src y = T.quotientMap.mapV a) : T.E :=
  (exists_quotientMap_mapE_eq_of_src_eq h).choose

private theorem src_liftDart {a : T.V} {y : T.quotient.E}
    (h : T.quotient.src y = T.quotientMap.mapV a) : T.src (liftDart h) = a :=
  (exists_quotientMap_mapE_eq_of_src_eq h).choose_spec.1

private theorem quotientMap_liftDart {a : T.V} {y : T.quotient.E}
    (h : T.quotient.src y = T.quotientMap.mapV a) : T.quotientMap.mapE (liftDart h) = y :=
  (exists_quotientMap_mapE_eq_of_src_eq h).choose_spec.2

/-- The end of the lift from `x₀` of a path of the quotient graph issuing from the image of `x₀`,
lifted dart by dart with `liftDart`. The lift of a path extended by a dart is the lift of the
path extended by a lift of that dart. -/
private noncomputable def liftPathEnd (x₀ : T.V) :
    ∀ {b : T.quotient.V}, T.quotient.Path (T.quotientMap.mapV x₀) b →
      {a : T.V // T.quotientMap.mapV a = b}
  | _, .nil => ⟨x₀, rfl⟩
  | _, .cons p f => ⟨T.tgt (liftDart (f.property.1.trans (liftPathEnd x₀ p).property.symm)), by
      rw [← Hom.map_tgt, quotientMap_liftDart, f.property.2]⟩

/-- The lifts of a path and of the path extended by a dart `f` are joined by a lift of `f`. -/
private theorem exists_liftPathEnd_cons (x₀ : T.V) {b c : T.quotient.V}
    (p : T.quotient.Path (T.quotientMap.mapV x₀) b) (f : Quiver.Hom b c) :
    ∃ e : T.E, T.src e = (liftPathEnd x₀ p).val ∧ T.quotientMap.mapE e = f.val ∧
      T.tgt e = (liftPathEnd x₀ (p.cons f)).val :=
  ⟨_, src_liftDart _, quotientMap_liftDart _, rfl⟩

/-- The lift of a spanning tree of the quotient graph: lifts of the vertices, with a prescribed
lift of one vertex, such that the two ends of every tree dart are joined by a lift of that dart.
The lifts are the ends of the lifts of the tree paths from the base vertex. -/
private theorem exists_lift_spanningTree (S : T.quotient.SpanningTree) (x₀ : T.V) :
    ∃ s : T.quotient.V → T.V, (∀ b, T.quotientMap.mapV (s b) = b) ∧
      s (T.quotientMap.mapV x₀) = x₀ ∧ ∀ y ∈ S.darts, ∃ e : T.E,
        T.src e = s (T.quotient.src y) ∧ T.tgt e = s (T.quotient.tgt y) ∧
          T.quotientMap.mapE e = y := by
  refine ⟨fun b => (liftPathEnd x₀ (S.path _ b)).val, fun b => (liftPathEnd x₀ _).property,
    by simp [liftPathEnd], fun y hy => ?_⟩
  rcases S.path_eq_cons_or_path_eq_cons_reverse (T.quotientMap.mapV x₀) (T.quotient.dart y)
    (by rwa [dart_val]) with h | h
  · obtain ⟨e, he₁, he₂, he₃⟩ := exists_liftPathEnd_cons x₀ _ (T.quotient.dart y)
    rw [← h] at he₃
    exact ⟨e, he₁, he₃, by rwa [dart_val] at he₂⟩
  · -- The tree path to the source of `y` passes through its target.
    obtain ⟨e, he₁, he₂, he₃⟩ :=
      exists_liftPathEnd_cons x₀ _ (Quiver.reverse (T.quotient.dart y))
    rw [← h] at he₃
    exact ⟨T.rev e, by rwa [src_rev], by rwa [tgt_rev], by simp [he₂]⟩

open scoped Classical in
/-- A lifting built from lifts `e y` of all darts `y` issuing from the lifts of their sources and
ending at the translates by elements `g y` of the lifts of their targets, with `g` trivial on the
spanning tree: the lift of the chosen dart `GeomEdge.out` of each geometric edge is kept, and the
lift of the other dart is the translate of the reverse of the kept one. -/
private noncomputable def Lifting.ofLifts (S : T.quotient.SpanningTree) (s : T.quotient.V → T.V)
    (e : T.quotient.E → T.E) (g : T.quotient.E → G) (hs : ∀ b, T.quotientMap.mapV (s b) = b)
    (he₁ : ∀ y, T.src (e y) = s (T.quotient.src y)) (he₂ : ∀ y, T.quotientMap.mapE (e y) = y)
    (he₃ : ∀ y, T.tgt (e y) = g y • s (T.quotient.tgt y)) (hg : ∀ y ∈ S.darts, g y = 1) :
    T.Lifting where
  tree := S
  vertex := s
  dart y := if GeomEdge.out T.quotient (T.quotient.toGeomEdge y) = y then e y
    else (g (T.quotient.rev y))⁻¹ • T.rev (e (T.quotient.rev y))
  twist y := if GeomEdge.out T.quotient (T.quotient.toGeomEdge y) = y then g y
    else (g (T.quotient.rev y))⁻¹
  quotientMap_vertex := hs
  quotientMap_dart y := by split_ifs <;> simp [he₂]
  src_dart y := by split_ifs <;> simp [he₁, he₃]
  twist_smul_dart_rev y := by
    rcases GeomEdge.out_toGeomEdge_eq_or_eq_rev T.quotient y with h | h <;>
      simp [h, T.quotient.rev_ne y, (T.quotient.rev_ne y).symm]
  twist_rev y := by
    rcases GeomEdge.out_toGeomEdge_eq_or_eq_rev T.quotient y with h | h <;>
      simp [h, T.quotient.rev_ne y, (T.quotient.rev_ne y).symm]
  twist_eq_one y hy := by split_ifs <;> simp [hg y hy, hg _ (S.rev_mem y hy)]

variable (T)

/-- For every spanning tree of the quotient graph and every vertex `x₀` of the tree there is a
lifting with that spanning tree in which the image of `x₀` lifts to `x₀`. -/
theorem exists_lifting (S : T.quotient.SpanningTree) (x₀ : T.V) :
    ∃ D : T.Lifting, D.tree = S ∧ D.vertex (T.quotientMap.mapV x₀) = x₀ := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hs₀, hsS⟩ := exists_lift_spanningTree S x₀
  -- Every dart has a lift issuing from the lift of its source and ending at a translate of the
  -- lift of its target, by the trivial element for the darts of the spanning tree.
  have key (y : T.quotient.E) : ∃ c : T.E × G, T.src c.1 = s (T.quotient.src y) ∧
      T.quotientMap.mapE c.1 = y ∧ T.tgt c.1 = c.2 • s (T.quotient.tgt y) ∧
        (y ∈ S.darts → c.2 = 1) := by
    by_cases hy : y ∈ S.darts
    · obtain ⟨e, he₁, he₂, he₃⟩ := hsS y hy
      exact ⟨(e, 1), he₁, he₃, by rw [he₂, one_smul], fun _ => rfl⟩
    · obtain ⟨e, he₁, he₂⟩ := exists_quotientMap_mapE_eq_of_src_eq (hs (T.quotient.src y)).symm
      obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : ∃ g : G, g • s (T.quotient.tgt y) = T.tgt e :=
        quotientMap_mapV_eq_iff.mp (by rw [hs, ← Hom.map_tgt, he₂])
      exact ⟨(e, g), he₁, he₂, hg.symm, fun h => absurd h hy⟩
  choose c hc₁ hc₂ hc₃ hc₄ using key
  exact ⟨Lifting.ofLifts S s (fun y => (c y).1) (fun y => (c y).2) hs hc₁ hc₂ hc₃ hc₄, rfl, hs₀⟩

variable {T} in
/-- Every `G`-tree has a lifting of its quotient graph. -/
instance : Nonempty T.Lifting :=
  (T.quotient.exists_spanningTree T.quotient_connected).map fun S =>
    (T.exists_lifting S (Classical.arbitrary T.V)).choose

namespace Lifting

variable {T} (D : T.Lifting)

/-- The lift of a dart ends at the translate by its element of the lift of its target. -/
@[simp] theorem tgt_dart (y : T.quotient.E) :
    T.tgt (D.dart y) = D.twist y • D.vertex (T.quotient.tgt y) := by
  simpa using (congrArg T.src (D.twist_smul_dart_rev y)).symm

/-- The lift of the reverse of a dart is the translate by the inverse of its element of the
reverse of its lift. -/
theorem dart_rev (y : T.quotient.E) :
    D.dart (T.quotient.rev y) = (D.twist y)⁻¹ • T.rev (D.dart y) :=
  eq_inv_smul_iff.mpr (D.twist_smul_dart_rev y)

/-- The lift of a dart of the spanning tree ends at the lift of its target. -/
theorem tgt_dart_of_mem {y : T.quotient.E} (hy : y ∈ D.tree.darts) :
    T.tgt (D.dart y) = D.vertex (T.quotient.tgt y) := by
  simp [hy]

/-- The lifts of the darts of the spanning tree are closed under reversal. -/
@[simp] theorem dart_rev_of_mem {y : T.quotient.E} (hy : y ∈ D.tree.darts) :
    D.dart (T.quotient.rev y) = T.rev (D.dart y) := by
  simp [dart_rev, hy]

/-- Distinct vertices of the quotient graph have distinct lifts. -/
theorem vertex_injective : Function.Injective D.vertex :=
  Function.LeftInverse.injective D.quotientMap_vertex

/-- Distinct darts of the quotient graph have distinct lifts. -/
theorem dart_injective : Function.Injective D.dart :=
  Function.LeftInverse.injective D.quotientMap_dart

@[simp] theorem vertex_inj {b₁ b₂ : T.quotient.V} : D.vertex b₁ = D.vertex b₂ ↔ b₁ = b₂ :=
  D.vertex_injective.eq_iff

@[simp] theorem dart_inj {y₁ y₂ : T.quotient.E} : D.dart y₁ = D.dart y₂ ↔ y₁ = y₂ :=
  D.dart_injective.eq_iff

/-- Every dart issuing from a lifted vertex is a translate, by an element of the stabilizer of
that vertex, of the lift of its image. -/
theorem exists_smul_dart_eq {b : T.quotient.V} {e : T.E} (he : T.src e = D.vertex b) :
    ∃ g ∈ stabilizer G (D.vertex b), g • D.dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e) = e := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := quotientMap_mapE_eq_iff.mp (D.quotientMap_dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e))
  refine ⟨g, mem_stabilizer_iff.mpr ?_, hg⟩
  simpa [he] using congrArg T.src hg

/-- The stabilizer of the lift of a dart `y` is contained in the stabilizer of the lift of the
source of `y`. -/
theorem stabilizer_dart_le_stabilizer_vertex (y : T.quotient.E) :
    stabilizer G (D.dart y) ≤ stabilizer G (D.vertex (T.quotient.src y)) :=
  D.src_dart y ▸ T.stabilizer_dart_le_stabilizer_src (D.dart y)

/-- The stabilizer of the lift of the reverse of `y` is contained in the stabilizer of the lift of
the target of `y`. -/
theorem stabilizer_dart_rev_le_stabilizer_vertex (y : T.quotient.E) :
    stabilizer G (D.dart (T.quotient.rev y)) ≤ stabilizer G (D.vertex (T.quotient.tgt y)) :=
  T.quotient.src_rev y ▸ D.stabilizer_dart_le_stabilizer_vertex (T.quotient.rev y)

/-- Conjugation by `(D.twist y)⁻¹` carries the stabilizer of `D.dart y` onto the stabilizer of
`D.dart (rev y)`. -/
theorem stabilizer_dart_rev (y : T.quotient.E) :
    stabilizer G (D.dart (T.quotient.rev y)) =
      (stabilizer G (D.dart y)).map (MulAut.conj (D.twist y)⁻¹).toMonoidHom := by
  rw [D.dart_rev, stabilizer_smul_eq_stabilizer_map_conj, T.stabilizer_rev]

/-- Conjugation by `D.twist y` carries the stabilizer of `D.dart (rev y)` onto the stabilizer of
`D.dart y`. -/
theorem stabilizer_dart (y : T.quotient.E) :
    stabilizer G (D.dart y) =
      (stabilizer G (D.dart (T.quotient.rev y))).map (MulAut.conj (D.twist y)).toMonoidHom := by
  simpa [D.twist_rev] using D.stabilizer_dart_rev (T.quotient.rev y)

/-- The subgroup of `G` generated by the stabilizers of the lifted vertices and the twist elements
of a lifting is the whole group `G`. -/
theorem iSup_stabilizer_sup_closure_range_twist :
    (⨆ b, stabilizer G (D.vertex b)) ⊔ Subgroup.closure (Set.range D.twist) = ⊤ := by
  let R : Subgroup G := (⨆ b, stabilizer G (D.vertex b)) ⊔ Subgroup.closure (Set.range D.twist)
  have hstab (b : T.quotient.V) : stabilizer G (D.vertex b) ≤ R :=
    le_sup_of_le_left (le_iSup (fun b => stabilizer G (D.vertex b)) b)
  have htwist (y : T.quotient.E) : D.twist y ∈ R :=
    Subgroup.mem_sup_right (Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨y, rfl⟩)
  -- Every vertex connected by a path in `T` to a lifted vertex is in the `R`-orbit of a lifted
  -- vertex.
  have hpath : ∀ {u v : T.V}, T.Path u v → (∃ r ∈ R, ∃ b, r • D.vertex b = u) →
      ∃ r ∈ R, ∃ b, r • D.vertex b = v := by
    intro u v p hu
    induction p with
    | nil => exact hu
    | @cons w z _ f ih =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, b, hrb⟩ := ih
      have hsrc : T.src (r⁻¹ • f.val) = D.vertex b := by
        rw [src_smul, f.property.1, ← hrb, inv_smul_smul]
      obtain ⟨h, hh, hdart⟩ := D.exists_smul_dart_eq hsrc
      refine ⟨r * h * D.twist (T.quotientMap.mapE (r⁻¹ • f.val)),
        mul_mem (mul_mem hr (hstab b hh)) (htwist _),
        T.quotient.tgt (T.quotientMap.mapE (r⁻¹ • f.val)), ?_⟩
      calc (r * h * D.twist (T.quotientMap.mapE (r⁻¹ • f.val))) •
            D.vertex (T.quotient.tgt (T.quotientMap.mapE (r⁻¹ • f.val)))
          = r • h • T.tgt (D.dart (T.quotientMap.mapE (r⁻¹ • f.val))) := by
            rw [D.tgt_dart, mul_smul, mul_smul]
        _ = r • T.tgt (r⁻¹ • f.val) := by rw [← tgt_smul, hdart]
        _ = z := by rw [tgt_smul, smul_inv_smul, f.property.2]
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  intro g _
  let b₀ : T.quotient.V := T.quotientMap.mapV (Classical.arbitrary T.V)
  obtain ⟨p⟩ := T.nonempty_path (D.vertex b₀) (g • D.vertex b₀)
  obtain ⟨r, hr, b, hrb⟩ := hpath p ⟨1, one_mem R, b₀, one_smul G _⟩
  have hb : b = b₀ := by
    have := congrArg T.quotientMap.mapV hrb
    simpa using this
  subst hb
  have hrg : r⁻¹ * g ∈ stabilizer G (D.vertex b₀) := by
    rw [mem_stabilizer_iff, mul_smul, inv_smul_eq_iff, hrb]
  simpa using mul_mem hr (hstab b₀ hrg)

/-! ### The graph of cosets -/

/-- An element of the group carrying the lift of the image of a dart to that dart. -/
private noncomputable def toDart (e : T.E) : G :=
  (quotientMap_mapE_eq_iff.mp (D.quotientMap_dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e))).choose

private theorem toDart_smul (e : T.E) : D.toDart e • D.dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e) = e :=
  (quotientMap_mapE_eq_iff.mp (D.quotientMap_dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e))).choose_spec

variable (K : T.quotient.V → Subgroup G)

/-- The graph of cosets of a family of subgroups `K b` indexed by the vertices of the quotient
graph: its vertices are the pairs of a vertex `b` of the quotient graph and a left coset of
`K b ⊓ G_{D.vertex b}`, and its darts are those of the tree, a dart `e` issuing from the coset at
the image of its source of an element carrying the lift of the image of `e` to `e`. -/
private noncomputable def cosetGraph : SerreGraph.{max u w, v} where
  V := Σ b : T.quotient.V, G ⧸ (K b ⊓ stabilizer G (D.vertex b))
  E := T.E
  src e := Sigma.mk (T.quotient.src (T.quotientMap.mapE e)) (QuotientGroup.mk (D.toDart e))
  rev := T.rev
  rev_rev := T.rev_rev
  rev_ne := T.rev_ne

/-- The coset of `g` at the vertex `b` of the quotient graph, as a vertex of the graph of
cosets. -/
private def cosetVertex (b : T.quotient.V) (g : G) : (D.cosetGraph K).V :=
  Sigma.mk b (QuotientGroup.mk g)

/-- A dart of the tree, as a dart of the graph of cosets. -/
private def cosetDart (e : T.E) : (D.cosetGraph K).E := e

private theorem cosetVertex_eq_cosetVertex_iff {b : T.quotient.V} {g g' : G} :
    D.cosetVertex K b g = D.cosetVertex K b g' ↔ g⁻¹ * g' ∈ K b ⊓ stabilizer G (D.vertex b) :=
  ⟨fun h => QuotientGroup.eq.mp
      (sigma_mk_injective (β := fun b => G ⧸ (K b ⊓ stabilizer G (D.vertex b))) h),
    fun h => congrArg (Sigma.mk b) (QuotientGroup.eq.mpr h)⟩

private theorem cosetGraph_rev_cosetDart (e : T.E) :
    (D.cosetGraph K).rev (D.cosetDart K e) = D.cosetDart K (T.rev e) :=
  rfl

/-- The morphism from the graph of cosets to the tree, sending the coset of `g` at `b` to
`g • D.vertex b`, and the identity on darts. -/
private noncomputable def cosetGraphHom : (D.cosetGraph K).Hom T.toSerreGraph where
  mapV x := ofQuotientStabilizer G (D.vertex x.1) (Subgroup.quotientMapOfLE inf_le_right x.2)
  mapE e := e
  map_src e := by
    have h := congrArg T.src (D.toDart_smul e)
    rwa [src_smul, src_dart, eq_comm] at h
  map_rev _ := rfl

private theorem cosetGraphHom_mapV_cosetVertex (b : T.quotient.V) (g : G) :
    (D.cosetGraphHom K).mapV (D.cosetVertex K b g) = g • D.vertex b :=
  rfl

variable {D K}

/-- The source of the translate by `g` of a lifted dart `y` is the coset of `g` at the source of
`y`, if `K` contains the stabilizer of the lifted dart. -/
private theorem cosetGraph_src {y : T.quotient.E}
    (hy : stabilizer G (D.dart y) ≤ K (T.quotient.src y)) {e : T.E} {g : G} (h : g • D.dart y = e) :
    (D.cosetGraph K).src (D.cosetDart K e) = D.cosetVertex K (T.quotient.src y) g := by
  obtain rfl : T.quotientMap.mapE e = y := by simp [← h]
  have hmem : (D.toDart e)⁻¹ * g ∈ stabilizer G (D.dart (T.quotientMap.mapE e)) := by
    rw [mem_stabilizer_iff, mul_smul, h, inv_smul_eq_iff, D.toDart_smul]
  have hsrc := T.stabilizer_dart_le_stabilizer_src _ hmem
  rw [src_dart] at hsrc
  exact congrArg (Sigma.mk _) (QuotientGroup.eq.mpr ⟨hy hmem, hsrc⟩)

/-- The target of the translate by `g` of a lifted dart `y` is the coset of `g * D.twist y` at
the target of `y`, if `K` contains the stabilizer of the lift of the reverse of `y`. -/
private theorem cosetGraph_tgt {y : T.quotient.E}
    (hy : stabilizer G (D.dart (T.quotient.rev y)) ≤ K (T.quotient.src (T.quotient.rev y)))
    {e : T.E} {g : G} (h : g • D.dart y = e) :
    (D.cosetGraph K).tgt (D.cosetDart K e) =
      D.cosetVertex K (T.quotient.tgt y) (g * D.twist y) := by
  rw [tgt_def, cosetGraph_rev_cosetDart, cosetGraph_src hy (e := T.rev e)
    (by rw [mul_smul, D.twist_smul_dart_rev, ← rev_smul, h]), src_rev]

variable {Y : Set T.quotient.E} (hY : ∀ y ∈ Y, T.quotient.rev y ∈ Y)
  (hdart : ∀ y ∈ Y, stabilizer G (D.dart y) ≤ K (T.quotient.src y))
include hY hdart

/-- A path of the spanning tree of the quotient graph with darts in `Y` lifts to a path of the
graph of cosets between the cosets of any fixed element. -/
private theorem nonempty_cosetGraph_path (g : G) {a c : T.quotient.V} (p : T.quotient.Path a c)
    (hp : ∀ y ∈ Path.darts T.quotient p, y ∈ Y ∧ y ∈ D.tree.darts) :
    Nonempty ((D.cosetGraph K).Path (D.cosetVertex K a g) (D.cosetVertex K c g)) := by
  induction p with
  | nil => exact ⟨.nil⟩
  | cons p y ih =>
    obtain ⟨q⟩ := ih fun z hz => hp z (by simp [hz])
    obtain ⟨y, rfl, rfl⟩ := y
    obtain ⟨hyY, hyS⟩ := hp y (by simp)
    exact ⟨q.cons ⟨D.cosetDart K (g • D.dart y), cosetGraph_src (hdart y hyY) rfl,
      by rw [cosetGraph_tgt (hdart _ (hY y hyY)) rfl, D.twist_eq_one y hyS, mul_one]⟩⟩

variable {R : Set T.quotient.V} {b₀ : T.quotient.V}
  (hR : ∀ b ∈ R, ∃ p : T.quotient.Path b₀ b,
    ∀ y ∈ Path.darts T.quotient p, y ∈ Y ∧ y ∈ D.tree.darts)
include hR

/-- The cosets of `h` and of `h * x` at `b₀` are joined in the graph of cosets if `x` lies in
`K b` for some `b` in `R`. -/
private theorem nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul_of_mem (hK : ∀ b ∈ R, K b ≤ stabilizer G (D.vertex b))
    {b : T.quotient.V} (hb : b ∈ R) {x : G} (hx : x ∈ K b) (h : G) :
    Nonempty ((D.cosetGraph K).Path (D.cosetVertex K b₀ h) (D.cosetVertex K b₀ (h * x))) := by
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hR b hb
  obtain ⟨q₁⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart h p hp
  obtain ⟨q₂⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart (h * x) p hp
  have hbx : D.cosetVertex K b h = D.cosetVertex K b (h * x) :=
    (cosetVertex_eq_cosetVertex_iff _ _).mpr
      (by rw [inv_mul_cancel_left]; exact Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hx, hK b hb hx⟩)
  rw [hbx] at q₁
  exact ⟨q₁.comp q₂.reverse⟩

/-- The cosets of `h` and of `h * D.twist y` at `b₀` are joined in the graph of cosets if `y`
lies in `Y`. -/
private theorem nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul_twist (hYR : ∀ y ∈ Y, T.quotient.src y ∈ R)
    {y : T.quotient.E} (hy : y ∈ Y) (h : G) :
    Nonempty ((D.cosetGraph K).Path (D.cosetVertex K b₀ h)
      (D.cosetVertex K b₀ (h * D.twist y))) := by
  obtain ⟨p₁, hp₁⟩ := hR _ (hYR y hy)
  obtain ⟨p₂, hp₂⟩ := hR _ (hYR _ (hY y hy))
  obtain ⟨q₁⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart h p₁ hp₁
  obtain ⟨q₂⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart (h * D.twist y) p₂ hp₂
  exact ⟨(q₁.cons ⟨D.cosetDart K (h • D.dart y), cosetGraph_src (hdart y hy) rfl,
    cosetGraph_tgt (hdart _ (hY y hy)) rfl⟩).comp q₂.reverse⟩

/-- If the subgroups `K b` for `b` in `R` and the elements attached to the darts of `Y` generate
the group, then the cosets of `h` and of `h * g` at `b₀` are joined in the graph of cosets. -/
private theorem nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul (hYR : ∀ y ∈ Y, T.quotient.src y ∈ R)
    (hK : ∀ b ∈ R, K b ≤ stabilizer G (D.vertex b))
    (hgen : Subgroup.closure ((⋃ b ∈ R, (K b : Set G)) ∪ D.twist '' Y) = ⊤) (g h : G) :
    Nonempty ((D.cosetGraph K).Path (D.cosetVertex K b₀ h) (D.cosetVertex K b₀ (h * g))) := by
  have hg : g ∈ Subgroup.closure ((⋃ b ∈ R, (K b : Set G)) ∪ D.twist '' Y) :=
    hgen ▸ Subgroup.mem_top g
  induction hg using Subgroup.closure_induction generalizing h with
  | mem x hx =>
    rcases hx with hx | ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    · obtain ⟨b, hb, hx⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp hx
      exact nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul_of_mem hY hdart hR hK hb hx h
    · exact nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul_twist hY hdart hR hYR hy h
  | one => rw [mul_one]; exact ⟨.nil⟩
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨q₁⟩ := ihx h
    obtain ⟨q₂⟩ := ihy (h * x)
    rw [mul_assoc] at q₂
    exact ⟨q₁.comp q₂⟩
  | inv x _ ihx =>
    obtain ⟨q⟩ := ihx (h * x⁻¹)
    rw [inv_mul_cancel_right] at q
    exact ⟨q.reverse⟩

omit hY hdart hR

variable (D) in
/-- Let `R` be a set of vertices of the quotient graph and `Y` a set of darts of the quotient
graph, closed under reversal and issuing from vertices of `R`, such that every vertex of `R` is
joined to a vertex `b₀` by a path in the spanning tree with darts in `Y`. For `b` in `R` let `K b`
be a subgroup of the stabilizer of the lifted vertex containing the stabilizers of the lifted
darts of `Y` issuing from it. If these subgroups and the elements attached to the darts of `Y`
generate the group, then `K b` is the whole stabilizer of the lifted vertex for every `b` in
`R`. -/
theorem eq_stabilizer_vertex_of_closure_eq_top {R : Set T.quotient.V} {Y : Set T.quotient.E}
    (hY : ∀ y ∈ Y, T.quotient.rev y ∈ Y) (hYR : ∀ y ∈ Y, T.quotient.src y ∈ R) {b₀ : T.quotient.V}
    (hR : ∀ b ∈ R, ∃ p : T.quotient.Path b₀ b,
      ∀ y ∈ Path.darts T.quotient p, y ∈ Y ∧ y ∈ D.tree.darts) (K : T.quotient.V → Subgroup G)
    (hK : ∀ b ∈ R, K b ≤ stabilizer G (D.vertex b))
    (hdart : ∀ y ∈ Y, stabilizer G (D.dart y) ≤ K (T.quotient.src y))
    (hgen : Subgroup.closure ((⋃ b ∈ R, (K b : Set G)) ∪ D.twist '' Y) = ⊤) {b : T.quotient.V}
    (hb : b ∈ R) : K b = stabilizer G (D.vertex b) := by
  refine le_antisymm (hK b hb) fun g hg => ?_
  -- The cosets of `g` and of `1` at `b` are joined in the graph of cosets and have the same
  -- image in the tree, so they are equal.
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hR b hb
  obtain ⟨q₁⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart g p hp
  obtain ⟨q₂⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path hY hdart 1 p hp
  obtain ⟨q₃⟩ := nonempty_cosetGraph_path_mul hY hdart hR hYR hK hgen g 1
  rw [one_mul] at q₃
  have := (D.cosetGraphHom K).eq_of_mapV_eq_of_isAcyclic T.isAcyclic (fun _ _ _ h => h)
    ((q₁.reverse.comp q₃.reverse).comp q₂) (by
      rw [cosetGraphHom_mapV_cosetVertex, cosetGraphHom_mapV_cosetVertex,
        mem_stabilizer_iff.mp hg, one_smul])
  simpa using ((cosetVertex_eq_cosetVertex_iff _ _).mp this).1

end Lifting

